1. **A computer-implemented method**, comprising:  
   receiving, by one or more computing devices of a service provider network, a request to process data generated by a plurality of Internet-of-Things (IoT) devices associated with a customer;  
   determining, based at least in part on one or more placement criteria, an edge computing system from among a plurality of edge computing systems, wherein the selected edge computing system is co-located in a provider-managed facility with network access equipment configured to receive traffic from at least a subset of the plurality of IoT devices;  
   provisioning, at the selected edge computing system, one or more computing resources configured to perform a data processing operation on IoT data received from the plurality of IoT devices;  
   generating an application programming interface (API) endpoint associated with the provisioned one or more computing resources;  
   causing configuration information identifying the API endpoint to be made available to the plurality of IoT devices or to a gateway device associated with the plurality of IoT devices;  
   receiving, via the API endpoint, IoT data from at least one IoT device of the plurality of IoT devices; and  
   processing the received IoT data at the selected edge computing system to generate processed IoT data.

2. **The computer-implemented method of claim 1**, wherein the one or more placement criteria comprise at least one of: geographic proximity to the plurality of IoT devices, network latency, available compute capacity, available storage capacity, a data residency requirement, a customer policy, a cost metric, or a reliability metric.

3. **The computer-implemented method of claim 1**, wherein the provider-managed facility comprises a telecommunications facility, a network aggregation facility, a cable headend, a central office, a radio access network facility, a content delivery facility, or a point-of-presence facility.

4. **The computer-implemented method of claim 1**, wherein provisioning the one or more computing resources comprises instantiating at least one of: a virtual machine, a container, a serverless function, a stream processing application, a machine learning inference service, or a data filtering service.

5. **The computer-implemented method of claim 1**, further comprising authenticating the at least one IoT device based at least in part on credentials associated with the API endpoint.

6. **The computer-implemented method of claim 1**, further comprising transmitting at least a portion of the processed IoT data from the selected edge computing system to a regional data center of the service provider network.

7. **The computer-implemented method of claim 1**, wherein processing the received IoT data comprises at least one of filtering, aggregation, normalization, compression, encryption, anomaly detection, event detection, machine learning inference, or protocol translation.

8. **The computer-implemented method of claim 1**, further comprising monitoring operational metrics of the selected edge computing system and, based at least in part on the operational metrics, migrating the data processing operation to a different edge computing system of the plurality of edge computing systems.

9. **The computer-implemented method of claim 1**, wherein causing the configuration information identifying the API endpoint to be made available comprises sending the configuration information to an IoT device registry, a device management service, or a customer management console.

10. **The computer-implemented method of claim 1**, wherein the API endpoint is configured to expose a protocol-specific interface for receiving IoT data using at least one of MQTT, HTTP, CoAP, AMQP, WebSocket, TCP, or UDP.

11. **A system**, comprising:  
    one or more processors; and  
    one or more memories storing instructions that, when executed by the one or more processors, cause the system to:  
    receive a request to establish distributed processing for IoT data generated by a set of IoT devices;  
    select, from among a plurality of edge computing systems deployed in provider-managed facilities, a particular edge computing system for processing the IoT data;  
    allocate compute capacity at the particular edge computing system for a customer-defined or provider-defined IoT data processing workload;  
    create an API endpoint associated with the allocated compute capacity;  
    provide endpoint configuration information for routing IoT data from the set of IoT devices to the API endpoint; and  
    execute the IoT data processing workload at the particular edge computing system on IoT data received through the API endpoint.

12. **The system of claim 11**, wherein the particular edge computing system is connected to a local network path through which IoT data from the set of IoT devices is received without first traversing a regional cloud data center.

13. **The system of claim 11**, wherein the instructions further cause the system to enforce an access control policy specifying which IoT devices are authorized to invoke the API endpoint.

14. **The system of claim 11**, wherein the instructions further cause the system to associate the API endpoint with a domain name, network address, port, certificate, token, or device identity policy.

15. **The system of claim 11**, wherein the instructions further cause the system to dynamically scale the allocated compute capacity at the particular edge computing system based at least in part on a volume of IoT data received through the API endpoint.

16. **The system of claim 11**, wherein the IoT data processing workload is configured to generate a control message for transmission to at least one IoT device in response to detecting an event in the IoT data.

17. **One or more non-transitory computer-readable storage media** storing instructions that, when executed by one or more processors, cause the one or more processors to perform operations comprising:  
    identifying a plurality of candidate edge computing systems located in provider-managed facilities;  
    selecting one of the plurality of candidate edge computing systems to process IoT telemetry data for a customer based at least in part on a latency objective associated with the customer;  
    deploying an executable processing component to the selected edge computing system;  
    provisioning an API endpoint mapped to the executable processing component;  
    registering the API endpoint for use by one or more IoT devices;  
    receiving IoT telemetry data at the API endpoint; and  
    invoking the executable processing component at the selected edge computing system to process the IoT telemetry data.

18. **The one or more non-transitory computer-readable storage media of claim 17**, wherein registering the API endpoint comprises updating a device shadow, device profile, routing table, DNS record, service discovery record, or IoT device registry.

19. **The one or more non-transitory computer-readable storage media of claim 17**, wherein the operations further comprise buffering the IoT telemetry data at the selected edge computing system during a loss of connectivity to a regional service provider facility.

20. **The one or more non-transitory computer-readable storage media of claim 17**, wherein the operations further comprise applying a customer-specified data handling policy at the selected edge computing system before transmitting processed data to another computing facility.
